What is Modular & Prefabricated Construction?
Modular and prefabricated construction represents an innovative building methodology where structural components are manufactured off-site in controlled factory environments before transport and rapid assembly at the construction location. This approach delivers significant advantages over traditional construction through standardized processes that enhance quality control, reduce material waste by up to 90%, and enable up to 50% faster project completion timelines – crucial benefits as Europe faces both housing shortages and aggressive carbon reduction targets.
